From: OpenWrt HA build <local>
Subject: [PATCH] owsync: do not free the embedded state of an expired tombstone

database_update_from_scan() removes a tombstone older than
TOMBSTONE_TTL_MS (30 days) with file_state_free(&entry->state). The
state is embedded in the db_entry_t, so that call ends in free() on a
pointer into the middle of the entry, 8 bytes past its start on 64-bit
targets, before the entry itself is freed. That is undefined behaviour,
and musl's allocator traps on such a pointer. The database is not saved
before the crash, so every respawn reaches the same tombstone and
crashes again until procd gives up, and config sync stays down.

It takes a synced file that was deleted 30 days earlier, on either
node. Release the two strings of the embedded state instead, as
database_free() does.

Present in upstream v1.2.0 and v1.3.0.

--- a/src/state.c
+++ b/src/state.c
@@ -620,7 +620,10 @@ int database_update_from_scan(database_t *db, const char *root, file_filter_t *f
                         db->buckets[i] = next;
                     }
                     free(entry->path);
-                    file_state_free(&entry->state);
+                    /* state is embedded in the entry: release its strings
+                     * only, the entry itself is freed just below */
+                    free(entry->state.path);
+                    free(entry->state.hash);
                     free(entry);
                     db->entry_count--;
                     *dirty = true;
